==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[decapitalise]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/diːˈkæpɪtəlaɪz/}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|decapitaliz|ing}}

# {{transitive}} To [[uncapitalize]] {{gloss|[[convert]] the first letter (or more) of (something) from [[uppercase]] to [[lowercase]]}}.
# {{transitive|legal}} To remove (something's) status as a [[capital crime]]; to cause (something) to no longer be a [[capital]] crime.
#* '''2009''', Stuart Banner, ''The Death Penalty: an American history'', page 131:
#*: In 1801 Connecticut '''decapitalized''' arson, but only where no victim's life had been placed in danger.

====Synonyms====
* [[uncapitalize]]

